RU Python Course Content

Course title: Python
Course code: LET-REMA-LC2601
Course year: 2026-2027
EC: 6 (Periods 1 and 2)
Language: English
Lecturer and coordinator: Cristian Tejedor-García (cristian.tejedorgarcia@ru.nl)

The 'chapters' folder contains .ipynb scripts from the course material 'Think Python', named by their chapter numbers

The assignment folder contains .ipynb assignment scripts.

There are eight (8) assignments, four (4) for each part of the course. Each one of the assignment needs to be submitted
via Brightspace before its deadline. Students start working on this assignment during the tutorial session in class with
the teacher and their peers. Each assignment is scored on a scale from 0 to 10. The final grade for all assignments is
the average of the individual grades. The average score obtained in all assignments will be normalized into a [1-10]
scale, constituting the 20% of the final grade of the course
Note 1: Delayed submissions without justification will not count for the first opportunity assessment.
Note 2: A minimum score of 6 is necessary to pass the assignment grade on OSIRIS.


